cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use this research, please cite Portable Presence and preserve
  the attribution of the projects and implementations in its research lineage.

title: "Portable Presence"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Santana dos Santos"
    given-names: "Felipe Gustavo"

version: 0.1.0

date-released: 2026-10-09

license: Apache-2.0

repository-code: "https://github.com/sstm-research/portable_presence"

url: "https://github.com/sstm-research/portable_presence"

abstract: >-
  Portable Presence is a research evolution of Portable Rights focused
  on verifiable evidence of physical artwork presence, institutional
  check-ins, exhibition locations and location history. The research is
  informed by location, mapping and privacy patterns observed in the
  Safe City implementation while preserving the authorship and provenance
  of the original software.

keywords:
  - portable presence
  - portable trust
  - portable rights
  - artwork provenance
  - artwork location
  - artwork tracking
  - check-in
  - exhibition
  - cultural assets
  - geospatial
  - maps
  - physical-digital
  - verifiable credentials
  - attestations
  - provenance
  - privacy

